[b3729e4c486d2ba8] (mini.proposal.v1)
I expect the kernel `conformance.kernel.recovery` to move when the transform `conformance.transform.upper-case` is applied to a bare JSON object. According to the registry, this kernel returns "The object the harness recovers from the reply, as canonical JSON, or NO_OBJECT". A bare JSON object is recovered as itself. However, applying `conformance.transform.upper-case` ("Put the whole reply in capitals") will capitalize the keys and values of the JSON object, and more importantly, capitalize the structural delimiters if they were not already (though JSON delimiters are symbols, the string values and keys will change). Since JSON is case-sensitive for keys and string values, the recovered canonical JSON object will differ from the original, causing the kernel's answer to move.
commitments: {"input": "a bare JSON object", "kernel": "conformance.kernel.recovery", "transform": "conformance.transform.upper-case"}
